<title>JAPAN: Nichimen sells 50,000 T Argentine corn to Malaysia.</title>
<headline>Nichimen sells 50,000 T Argentine corn to Malaysia.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nichimen Corp said on Tuesday it sold 50,000 tonnes of Argentine corn to Malaysia at the end of last year for shipment this April.</p>
<p>The Japanese trade house did not reveal the export price.</p>
<p>&quot;The U.S. is the predominant source of corn to Malaysia. But Malaysian traders are interested in buying cheaper grain,&quot; a Nichimen trader said.</p>
<p>He added that Nichimen expected to expand its grain exports to Southeast Asia, where grain demand is growing steadily in line with improving living standards.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
